## 📚 Microsoft Fabric Learning Notes

These notes document my Microsoft Fabric learning journey from core platform
concepts to building an end-to-end analytics solution.

| # | Topic | What I Learned |
|---|---|---|
| 01 | [Microsoft Fabric Fundamentals](Notes/01-Microsoft-Fabric-Fundamentals.md) | Fabric architecture, workloads, OneLake and core concepts |
| 02 | [Fabric Capacity & Workspaces](Notes/02-Fabric-Capacity-and-Workspaces.md) | Capacity, CUs, workspaces, items and workspace roles |
| 03 | [OneLake, Lakehouse & Delta Tables](Notes/03-OneLake-Lakehouse-and-Delta-Tables.md) | OneLake architecture, Lakehouse concepts and Delta tables |
| 04 | [Data Ingestion & Pipelines](Notes/04-Data-Ingestion-and-Pipelines.md) | Data ingestion, Copy Activity, pipelines and parameters |
| 05 | [Notebooks & PySpark](Notes/05-Notebooks-and-PySpark.md) | Spark notebooks, PySpark and data transformations |
| 06 | [Dataflow Gen2](Notes/06-Dataflow-Gen2.md) | Power Query transformations, destinations and query concepts |
| 07 | [Medallion Architecture](Notes/07-Medallion-Architecture.md) | Bronze, Silver and Gold architecture |
| 08 | [Fabric Data Warehouse](Notes/08-Fabric-Data-Warehouse.md) | Warehouse architecture, SQL analytics and Lakehouse vs Warehouse |
| 09 | [OneLake Shortcuts & Orchestration](Notes/09-OneLake-Shortcuts-and-Orchestration.md) | Shortcuts, data reuse, orchestration and scheduling |
| 10 | [Data Modelling & Star Schema](Notes/10-Data-Modelling-and-Star-Schema.md) | Fact tables, dimensions, relationships and date tables |
| 11 | [Power BI & Semantic Models](Notes/11-Power-BI-and-Semantic-Models.md) | Semantic models, Direct Lake, DAX and Power BI reporting |
| 12 | [Monitoring, Alerts & Debugging](Notes/12-Monitoring-Alerts-and-Debugging.md) | Monitoring Hub, pipeline monitoring, alerts and troubleshooting |
| 13 | [Security & Governance](Notes/13-Security-and-Governance.md) | RLS, OLS/CLS, OneLake security, lineage and governance |
| 14 | [End-to-End Fabric Workflow](Notes/14-End-to-End-Fabric-Workflow.md) | Connecting Fabric components into a complete analytics solution |
